      <p style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#5a4636;margin:0 auto 30px;max-width:60ch;">Picture the next few months turned around: cool, steady days where the heat doesn't ambush you mid-sentence. Full nights on dry sheets, waking up rested. Your patience back. Your focus back. Yourself back. That isn't wishful thinking — it's what happens when you treat the root instead of the heat. I spent twenty-five years handing women the wrong advice. I won't do it again. If any of this sounds like your life — the mid-meeting flush, the 3am soaked sheets, the doctor who said your labs were "normal" — this was made for you.{{ wk_star }}</p>
