    {"type": "textarea", "id": "cta_quote", "label": "cta_quote", "default": "Our summer sale is live: save up to 51% with free shipping on all subscriptions — backed by our 90-day money-back guarantee."},
    {"type": "text", "id": "cta_bar1", "label": "cta_bar1", "default": "Up to 51% off"},
    {"type": "text", "id": "cta_bar2", "label": "cta_bar2", "default": "Free shipping on all subscriptions"},
    {"type": "text", "id": "cta_guarantee", "label": "cta_guarantee", "default": "Try it risk-free with our 90-day money-back guarantee."},
    {"type": "image_picker", "id": "cta_image", "label": "cta_image"},
    {"type": "header", "content": "Article hero"},
    {"type": "text", "id": "hero_eyebrow", "label": "hero_eyebrow"},
    {"type": "text", "id": "hero_h1_lead", "label": "hero_h1_lead", "default": "Why your hot flashes"},
    {"type": "text", "id": "hero_h1_accent", "label": "hero_h1_accent", "default": "aren't a heat problem"},
    {"type": "text", "id": "hero_h1_tail", "label": "hero_h1_tail", "default": "— and the gut-hormone shift that finally cooled them down"},
    {"type": "image_picker", "id": "hero_image", "label": "hero_image"},
    {"type": "image_picker", "id": "byline_image", "label": "byline_image"},
    {"type": "image_picker", "id": "story1_image", "label": "story1_image"},
    {"type": "image_picker", "id": "story2_image", "label": "story2_image"},
    {"type": "text", "id": "byline_name", "label": "byline_name", "default": "By Sarah Ellison, WHNP"},
    {"type": "text", "id": "byline_sub", "label": "byline_sub", "default": "Women's Health Nurse Practitioner · 25 Years in Women's Health"},
    {"type": "text", "id": "read_time", "label": "read_time", "default": "8 min read"},
    {"type": "textarea", "id": "hero_p1", "label": "hero_p1", "default": "I'm a women's health nurse. I spent 25 years telling women to dress in layers and wait it out. Then my own hot flashes hit — in the middle of a patient appointment — and I discovered everything I was taught was missing the real cause."},
    {"type": "textarea", "id": "hero_p2", "label": "hero_p2", "default": "The first time it truly floored me, I was mid-sentence with a patient."},
    {"type": "inline_richtext", "id": "hero_p3", "label": "hero_p3", "default": "Heat climbed my chest and neck like someone had opened an oven door inside me. My face went crimson. Sweat beaded at my hairline. I had to stop talking, grab a clipboard, and fan myself — in front of a woman who was there for <em>her</em> appointment, not mine."},
    {"type": "textarea", "id": "hero_p4", "label": "hero_p4", "default": "I mumbled something about the thermostat. But I knew."},
    {"type": "inline_richtext", "id": "hero_p5", "label": "hero_p5", "default": "I'm a women's health nurse practitioner. For twenty-five years, I'd handed women the same script: <em>\"It's just menopause. Dress in layers. Carry a fan. It'll pass.\"</em>"},
    {"type": "textarea", "id": "hero_p6", "label": "hero_p6", "default": "And there I stood — flushed, dripping, humiliated in my own clinic — realizing I'd been dismissing women for a quarter of a century, and nobody had ever told me what it actually felt like."},
    {"type": "text", "id": "story1_head", "label": "story1_head", "default": "It isn't the heat that takes the most from you."},
    {"type": "textarea", "id": "story1_p1", "label": "story1_p1", "default": "It's everything the heat steals."},
    {"type": "textarea", "id": "story1_p2", "label": "story1_p2", "default": "The flushes came a dozen times a day. During morning rounds. In the grocery line. At the dinner table with my husband, mid-sentence. My face would ignite without warning, sweat would roll down my back, and I'd quietly fan myself while pretending to follow the conversation."},
    {"type": "textarea", "id": "story1_p3", "label": "story1_p3", "default": "Then came the night sweats: 2am, sheets soaked through. Change. Lie awake, wired, heart racing. Finally drift off at 4:30 — and the alarm screams at 6."},
    {"type": "textarea", "id": "story1_p4", "label": "story1_p4", "default": "After a week of broken sleep, I couldn't hold a thought past 3pm. I snapped at my kids over nothing. I cried in the parking lot before work and couldn't explain why."},
    {"type": "textarea", "id": "story1_p5", "label": "story1_p5", "default": "I started mapping every AC vent in every building I entered. I dressed in layers I could strip off in a panic. I carried a portable fan in my purse. I became a woman who quietly shrank her life — turning down dinner invitations, avoiding crowded rooms, dreading anything that might trap me mid-flush in public."},
    {"type": "textarea", "id": "story1_p6", "label": "story1_p6", "default": "I didn't just lose my comfort. I lost my confidence, my patience, and — slowly — the sense of who I was."},
    {"type": "textarea", "id": "story1_p7", "label": "story1_p7", "default": "The woman who was sharp in meetings, present with her family, steady in her own skin — she was disappearing. And I didn't know how to get her back."},
    {"type": "text", "id": "hero_cta", "label": "hero_cta", "default": "Skip to what worked →"},
    {"type": "text", "id": "story2_head", "label": "story2_head", "default": "Then I did something I'd told hundreds of patients to do: I went to my doctor."},
    {"type": "inline_richtext", "id": "story2_p1", "label": "story2_p1", "default": "She's someone I'd known for fifteen years. A good doctor. She ran labs, called me two days later, and said: <em>\"Everything looks normal, Sarah. It's probably just stress. We could try a low-dose antidepressant if you want.\"</em>"},
    {"type": "inline_richtext", "id": "story2_p2", "label": "story2_p2", "default": "I sat in my car after that call and felt something I'd never understood in my patients before. <strong>Invisible. Dismissed. Like my suffering wasn't real enough to matter.</strong>"},
    {"type": "textarea", "id": "story2_p3", "label": "story2_p3", "default": "I had spent my career being the expert. And now I was the patient being told — by someone in my own profession — that my body's betrayal was \"probably just stress.\""},
    {"type": "textarea", "id": "story2_p4", "label": "story2_p4", "default": "I walked into that appointment a healthcare provider. I walked out a woman who finally understood what every patient I'd ever dismissed must have felt."},
    {"type": "header", "content": "Why it failed"},
    {"type": "text", "id": "fail_eyebrow", "label": "fail_eyebrow", "default": "Everything I tried first"},
    {"type": "text", "id": "fail_heading", "label": "fail_heading", "default": "I'm a nurse. I tried all of it — and it all failed the same way."},
    {"type": "textarea", "id": "fail_intro", "label": "fail_intro", "default": "Over eighteen months, I worked through the whole list — the same list I used to hand my patients. Here's what each thing cost me and exactly why it never touched the flashes. If you've tried these too, the failure was built into them, not into you."},
    {"type": "text", "id": "prob1_eyebrow", "label": "prob1_eyebrow", "default": "The \"menopause\" gummy · $32"},
    {"type": "text", "id": "prob1_title", "label": "prob1_title", "default": "The gummy that quietly made the flashes worse"},
    {"type": "textarea", "id": "prob1_body", "label": "prob1_body", "default": "I bought the pretty bottle off the pharmacy shelf. What I didn't read — a nurse, embarrassingly — was the 3g of sugar per serving. Sugar throws off the gut bacteria that keep your estrogen steady, and unstable estrogen is exactly what triggers the flush. I was paying to feed the problem."},
