    {"type": "inline_richtext", "id": "disc_p2", "label": "disc_p2", "default": "But that led to the question I'd never once been taught to ask in twenty-five years on the ward: <strong>why was the estrogen swinging so violently in the first place?</strong> The answer wasn't in my ovaries. It was in my gut."},
    {"type": "inline_richtext", "id": "disc_p4", "label": "disc_p4", "default": "And here's the part that made me furious: <strong>sugar feeds the exact microbes that throw the estrobolome off balance.</strong> Every sweet \"menopause gummy\" I'd ever recommended had been quietly making the flashes worse."},
    {"type": "textarea", "id": "disc_p5", "label": "disc_p5", "default": "Nothing is wrong with you. The gut-hormone axis is broken. And nobody — not your doctor, not the pharmacy shelf, not the $140 drawer of cooling gadgets — is addressing it."},
    {"type": "text", "id": "disc2_head", "label": "disc2_head", "default": "That's when I found Womankind — or rather, a colleague told me who built it."},
    {"type": "textarea", "id": "disc2_p1", "label": "disc2_p1", "default": "She's an OB/GYN I'd referred patients to for years. Over coffee, I mentioned the flashes. She didn't tell me to dress in layers."},
    {"type": "inline_richtext", "id": "disc2_p2", "label": "disc2_p2", "default": "She said: <em>\"A former colleague of ours — Dr. Katie Chen — got so tired of watching her patients get dismissed that she formulated something herself. Board-certified OB/GYN. Menopause Society credentialed. She spent years in clinic watching women in their early forties arrive flushed, exhausted, and told their labs were 'normal.' The shelf was empty — nothing combined researched-dose botanicals with the probiotic strains that actually support the estrobolome. So she built it.\"</em>"},
    {"type": "inline_richtext", "id": "disc2_p3", "label": "disc2_p3", "default": "<strong>Dr. Katie Chen is exactly the kind of clinician you want formulating something you put in your body every day</strong> — someone who spent years on the other side of the exam table, ran out of things to recommend, and decided to solve the problem herself instead of shrugging and reaching for the prescription pad."},
    {"type": "textarea", "id": "disc2_p4", "label": "disc2_p4", "default": "I didn't want another cooling gadget. I wanted the formula that steadied the root. The one I found — the one Dr. Chen built — is called Womankind. They call the approach the Root-Up Method, because it works from the gut-hormone root up to the flush itself. After a career of quiet skepticism, it's the first supplement I've ever put my name to."},
